      <scoEntry>
        <scoEntryTitle>Component identification</scoEntryTitle>
        <para>This sharable content object teaches the location of the slat system components on the
          aircraft. It is used in the line maintenance familiarization course and takes about ten
          minutes to complete.</para>
        <scoEntry>
          <scoEntryTitle>Belly fairing components</scoEntryTitle>
          <para>The power control unit is installed between frame C41 and frame C44, on the left hand
            side of the centre line, and is reached through access panel 196AB.</para>
          <figure>
            <title>Slat system — component location</title>
            <graphic infoEntityIdent="ICN-A350X-A-278100-A-U8025-00001-A-001-01"/>
          </figure>
          <learningEvent learnEventCode="A">
            <para>On the illustration, select the power control unit. The learner has three attempts
              before the answer is shown.</para>
          </learningEvent>
        </scoEntry>
        <scoEntry>
          <scoEntryTitle>Wing components</scoEntryTitle>
          <para>The asymmetry position pick-off unit is at the outboard end of the transmission, at
            rib 14. It is reached only with the slats fully retracted and both hydraulic systems
            depressurized.</para>
          <learningEvent learnEventCode="B">
            <para>Order the four steps required to gain access to the asymmetry position pick-off
              unit. The learner may not continue until the order is correct.</para>
          </learningEvent>
        </scoEntry>
      </scoEntry>
    </scoContent>
